From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WS-B <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:02:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0983 redfin: /dev/cu.bluetooth etc. bridged to btd (btbridge)

New bsd/dev/sweet_btbridge.c (boot-arg btbridge=1, default: no nodes): a byte
pipe so iOS's Bluetooth stack reaches phone/bt/btd. /dev/cu.bluetooth and
/dev/uart.bluetooth are the H4 serial port bluetoothd opens (two names, one
pipe); /dev/btbridge is the other end that btd --bridge opens; /dev/btwake is
a dummy wake line that accepts everything. Two 16 KiB rings, blocking reads
(PCATCH), O_NONBLOCK and select()/poll() supported, host side one opener at a
time, rings cleared when btd opens btbridge. Nothing is interpreted here;
btd owns H4. Called from sweet_ufs.c after sweet_geniuart_init.


---
 bsd/conf/files           |   1 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_btbridge.c | 319 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c      |   2 +
 3 files changed, 322 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 bsd/dev/sweet_btbridge.c

